 use software like Macromedia's Dream Weaver, put it into 'Design View' and then struggle to float various content to the left or right of the page. After you were done you'd upload the files via FTP and hope that the slop on the server looked like the slop on your computer. It was awful. And it was beautiful.</p><p data-block-key=\\\\\\"9iic0\\\\\\">It also didn't hurt that the White Sox win the world series for the first time in 88 years. Suffice to say, if I block out the memories of low paying retail jobs and credit card debt, it was like living in the renaissance.</p><p data-block-key=\\\\\\"eq6aj\\\\\\"></p><p data-block-key=\\\\\\"a4l13\\\\\\">On this blog I intend to write about technology, especially especially sharing some of the nerdy things I learn during extensive meditation (ADHD hyper focus) sessions. I have a lot of fun messing around with python, JavaScript, and Linux. I also intend to write about project management, because truth is, technology doesn't usually solve problems, <i>great teams do</i>. Scattered here and there will be my various hobbies including cooking, bread making, cycling, video games, music, urban planning, language, vacation and of course, pictures of my cats! While I don't promise much, I'll always make this site ad free, with perhaps a Patreon account.</p><p data-block-key=\\\\\\"4cott\\\\\\"><b>About Me:</b></p><p data-block-key=\\\\\\"4240t\\\\\\">I grew up in Bayport, New York, a small, mostly flat suburban town sandwiched in between many other small suburban towns for miles in every direction (also known as Long Island). Every important skill, coping mechanism, and deleterious mistake I've made can be traced back to my banal, albeit traumatic existence living there. Despite completing multiple degrees, living in many cities across the US, Canada, and Europe - and having a very rewarding career in IT and libraries, part of me still feels like that lost teenager who learned every Nirvana song on guitar while simultaneously failing math. I currently work for a public library in the interior of British Columbia with my partner Alice, and our three cats Serge, Maisah, and Nala.</p><p data-block-key=\\\\\\"47oqe\\\\\\">If you've stumbled onto this site, I'd like to welcome you to it! I'm not sure how you got here without the magic of Google SEO, but I'm glad you got here anyway - and that's the important thing. Happy New Year!</p><p data-block-key=\\\\\\"6dr5l\\\\\\"></p><p data-block-key=\\\\\\"3nn5k\\\\\\"></p><p data-block-key=\\\\\\"f5guv\\\\\\"></p><p data-block-key=\\\\\\"8n6th\\\\\\"></p>\\", \\"id\\": \\"a28f90e6-1305-4bc1-aab9-3215fefce223\\"}]", "expired": false, "alias_of": null, "numchild": 0, "url_path": "/welcome/youre-blogging-in-2025/", "blog_date": "2025-01-02", "expire_at": null, "locked_at": null, "locked_by": null, "seo_title": "", "blog_image": 3, "go_live_at": null, "draft_title": "It's 2025, Blog like it's 2025!", "content_type": 44, "live_revision": 22, "show_in_menus": false, "latest_revision": 29, "translation_key": "2df69ac9-a9e1-4f59-b3bd-86a5630b411d", "last_published_at": "2025-01-05T01:33:55.156Z", "first_published_at": "2024-12-28T00:47:59.494Z", "search_description": "", "wagtail_admin_comments": [], "has_unpublished_changes": true, "latest_revision_created_at": "2025-01-05T02:31:39.403Z"}	\N	6	1	44	1	It's 2025, Blog like it's 2025!
